    "drug_interactions": "Digitalis glycosides, diltiazem, verapamil, and beta-blockers slow atrioventricular conduction and decrease heart rate. Concomitant use with negative chronotropes can increase the risk of bradycardia or hypotension [see Warnings and Precautions (5.2) ]. Coadministration of labetalol HCl with non-dihydropyridine calcium-channel antagonists (e.g., verapamil) is contraindicated [see Contraindications (4) ].",
