    "drug_name": "Clotrimazole and Betamethasone Dipropionate",
    "side_effects": "Use of topical corticosteroids may increase the risk of posterior subcapsular cataracts and glaucoma. Cataracts and glaucoma have been reported in postmarketing experience with the use of topical corticosteroid products, including topical betamethasone products [see Adverse Reactions (6.2) ]. Avoid contact of clotrimazole and betamethasone dipropionate cream, 1%/0.05% (base) with eyes. Advise patients to report any visual symptoms and consider referral to an ophthalmologist for evaluation.",
